--- machine\software\radius
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius

Configuration of the radiusd RADIUS authentication service.

Administrators own these keys; radiusd needs read and subtree-notify access.
It has no configuration-write authority. Configuration is watched and
revalidated periodically, including referenced files. Invalid, unreadable, or
pending configuration pauses successful admissions. Reads are deliberately
non-transactional for this milestone; concurrent edits can form a mixed but
valid configuration. Use administrative transactions for related changes.

--- machine\software\radius\settings
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings

Listener addresses and bounded authentication-conversation resources.

--- machine\software\radius\settings listen
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings Listen
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–16 distinct literal IPv4 or IPv6 socket addresses with nonzero ports
applies: live

UDP listeners, such as 0.0.0.0:1812 and [::]:1812.

IPv6 sockets are IPv6-only. Hostnames and mapped IPv6 addresses are refused.
The service SID also needs PORT_BIND in the normal port-reservation SD.
Changing the listener set cancels pending exchanges and cached replies.

--- machine\software\radius\settings idletimeoutseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings IdleTimeoutSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 30
valid: 1–3600
applies: live (new exchanges)

Maximum inactivity during an authentication conversation.

--- machine\software\radius\settings overalltimeoutseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings OverallTimeoutSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 120
valid: 1–3600
applies: live (new exchanges)

Fixed total conversation lifetime, including time spent waiting for authd.

Progress and configuration changes never extend an existing deadline.

--- machine\software\radius\settings replycacheseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings ReplyCacheSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 15
valid: 1–3600
applies: live (new cache entries)

Lifetime of exact retransmission replies.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxattempts
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxAttempts
type: REG_DWORD
default: 256
valid: 1–65536
applies: live

Global bound on allocated authentication conversations.

Lowering this bound stops new allocation without extending existing work.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxattemptsperclient
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxAttemptsPerClient
type: REG_DWORD
default: 32
valid: 1–65536
applies: live

Conversation allocation bound per trusted client definition.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxcachedreplies
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxCachedReplies
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1024
valid: 1–65536
applies: live

Maximum cached RADIUS replies; oldest entries are evicted at capacity.

--- machine\software\radius\settings fragmentbytes
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings FragmentBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1000
valid: 64–3000
applies: live (new exchanges)

Maximum outgoing EAP-TTLS fragment payload.

--- machine\software\radius\settings maxverifications
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Settings MaxVerifications
type: REG_DWORD
default: 32
valid: 1–MaxAttempts
applies: live

Maximum simultaneous asynchronous authd credential verifications.

At capacity a newly verification-ready attempt fails without keys. There is
no unbounded queue. Lowering the limit does not restart existing work.

--- machine\software\radius\tls
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\TLS

Server credentials for EAP-TTLS; individual client certificates are not required.

Provision immutable, administrator-owned, protected regular files. Referenced
files must be singly linked and are opened without following a final symlink.
Only SYSTEM or Administrators may modify credentials. radiusd can read them.
Use a protected parent directory as well. Public certificates can grant other
principals read/execute access; private keys and AP secrets cannot.

--- machine\software\radius\tls certificatefiles
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\TLS CertificateFiles
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–16 absolute paths to DER certificates, each at most 65536 bytes
applies: live (new exchanges)

Ordered certificate chain, starting with the server certificate.

Clients must trust its CA and validate the expected server name. A certificate
renewal changes new TLS exchanges while bounded existing exchanges complete.

--- machine\software\radius\tls privatekeyfile
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\TLS PrivateKeyFile
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: absolute path to an unencrypted DER private key, at most 65536 bytes
applies: live (new exchanges)

Protected private key matching the first certificate.

Write new protected files first, then transactionally switch references. Keep
old files until their references and any bounded readers have been released.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client>

A trusted RADIUS client definition, selected by the actual UDP source address.

Record identifiers contain 1–64 lowercase ASCII letters, digits, or hyphens.
At most 256 client definitions are accepted. The most-specific source prefix
wins. Equal duplicate prefixes are invalid. A bad secret never falls back to
a less-specific client. NAS attributes cannot select a trusted definition.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> addresses
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> Addresses
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–256 canonical literal IPv4/IPv6 addresses or CIDR prefixes
applies: live

Actual packet sources permitted to use this client's secret.

Prefixes with host bits and mapped IPv6 addresses are invalid. Trust edits
cancel affected pending exchanges and cached replies.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> secretfile
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> SecretFile
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: absolute path to a protected regular file containing 16–1024 secret bytes
applies: live

AP shared secret, read as exact bytes without trimming or newline removal.

Rotating it invalidates affected pending exchanges and cached replies. The
Registry contains the file reference rather than the shared secret itself.

--- machine\software\radius\clients\<client> networks
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Clients\<client> Networks
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (required)
valid: 1–256 existing network record identifiers with distinct SSIDs
applies: live

Networks this client may serve.

An initial request must carry an integrity-protected Called-Station-Id with a
valid MAC prefix and exact SSID. Missing, malformed, or unmapped names have no
fallback, even when only one network is allowed. A continuation keeps its
original binding; a supplied SSID must still match it.

--- machine\software\radius\networks\<network>
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Networks\<network>

A network admission policy, independent of identity verification in authd.

At most 256 networks are accepted. Record names follow the client-name rules.

--- machine\software\radius\networks\<network> ssid
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Networks\<network> SSID
type: REG_SZ
default: (required)
valid: nonempty UTF-8 text, at most 32 bytes
applies: live

Exact, case-sensitive SSID advertised by the AP.

Renaming an SSID invalidates conversations bound to the previous name.

--- machine\software\radius\networks\<network> connectsecurity
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Networks\<network> ConnectSecurity
type: REG_SZ or REG_BINARY
default: (required)
valid: SDDL or a validated self-relative security descriptor, at most 65536 bytes
applies: live (at final admission)

Ordinary security descriptor for the network's Connect right, mask 0x1.

Generic read, execute, and all map to Connect; generic write maps to zero.
Supply an owner. An absent DACL deliberately grants access; an empty DACL
denies it. Missing identity context, unsupported execution context, and SACL
audit requirements fail closed. The temporary userspace checker creates no
kernel token and cannot impersonate the user. Source groups are used as
returned by authd, without inventing local-session or built-in memberships.

--- machine\software\radius\networks\<network> reauthenticateseconds
canonical: Machine\Software\Radius\Networks\<network> ReauthenticateSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 3600
valid: 1–4294967295
applies: live (next successful admission)

Requested AP reauthentication interval, in seconds.

Access-Accept carries signed Session-Timeout and Termination-Action equal to
RADIUS-Request. This requests future authentication; it does not disconnect an
existing station immediately. Actual AP/client enforcement needs qualification.
